cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CrossAudit, please cite it as below."
title: "CrossAudit: A Git-Native, Cross-Vendor Audit Loop for Agentic Science"
authors:
  - family-names: "Dong"
    given-names: "Zhaohe"
type: software
year: 2026
url: "https://github.com/dongzhaohe321418-lab/crossaudit"
abstract: >-
  CrossAudit is a lightweight protocol for supervising autonomous AI research
  agents: every experiment increment produced by a generator agent is audited
  by an agent from a different model vendor against a versioned, human-authored
  rulebook, with git as the tamper-evident ledger, deterministic scripted checks
  as a model-free backstop, and bounded escalation to a human principal.
keywords:
  - agentic science
  - AI scientist
  - LLM auditing
  - self-preference bias
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
